{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Microservice.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Microservice.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"microservice microservice","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Microservice.md","fileName":"Microservice.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Microservice","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 22:09\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Containerized Microservice Architecture]] [[Cloud Scalability and Resilience Patterns]] [[.NET Server Concurrency and Parallel Patterns]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Containerized Microservice Architecture","Cloud Scalability and Resilience Patterns",".NET Server Concurrency and Parallel Patterns","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf","hands-onparallelprogrammingwithc8andnetcore3.pdf","hands-onrestfulwebserviceswithaspnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Microservice.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Microservice.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"microservice microservice","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Microservice.md","fileName":"Microservice.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Microservice","heading":"Microservice","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A microservice is a small, independently operated process responsible for a bounded capability. The order-processing example treats autonomy as the defining property: the worker can continue running even when no new orders arrive and does not require another application process to remain alive.\n\nIndependent deployment and scaling can isolate change, but dividing one system into many services adds network, versioning, logging, and data-consistency problems. The book cautions that a microservice architecture is useful only when those costs solve a real need.\n\nThe design-patterns source 